WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.962
The test stage is a go
when five things hold.

2
00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:07.225
Preflight passed, and the deployer's
rights read one, one, one.

3
00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:10.850
The three hashes in the change
record match the files that ran.

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.825
The parallel run printed
cutover-ready, N of N.

5
00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:17.123
Thirty days of observation
passed with no failed

6
00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:20.500
login on a disabled or denied
login, and no drift row.

7
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.950
And every deploy record
says applied, not dry run.

8
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.675
A no-go is a finding with an
owner, and the stage is repeated.

9
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:29.782
The seal re-hashes every run's files,

10
00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:34.504
refuses a stage missing a required step
or with a deploy run that wasn't applied,

11
00:00:34.504 --> 00:00:38.500
and appends one record to the chain
with the previous record's hash.

12
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.763
Sealed with the rehearsal
switch, it records a rehearsal,

13
00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:44.263
which production preflight never accepts.

14
00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:46.345
Production then runs the same steps,

15
00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.538
and its seal also needs the
closure record from Module 9.

16
00:00:49.538 --> 00:00:53.770
When Entra can't be reached, Appendix
B's path is the registered break-glass

17
00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.863
Windows group, empty by default, with
every membership change alerting.
